===Japanese Version===
*November 15th, 2022 to December 27th, 2022

==Trivia==
*All of these stages are exact copies of [[Season 1: School Days]] stages, with the exceptions of [[2014 Part 1]], [[2016 Part 1]], [[2018 Part 1]] and [[2021 Part 1]].
**The reason they were changed is likely because their respective stages included [[Gary Gory]].
*The map starts in 2012 with the release of the [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese Version]], but the [[The Battle Cats|English Version]] itself was released in 2014, so BCEN's version of this map skipped the years 2019 and 2022 in order for it to end on 2024, the year of the 10th anniversary of BCEN, without having to edit the map or create new stages.
*Because of regional differences as well as the 2019 and 2022 cut, the English version of the map omits the release of the Battle Cats' [[Gummy Cat (Special Cat)|gummies]] and [[Wafer Cat (Special Cat)|wafers]], the TV commercial promoting the 8th anniversary and the [https://youtu.be/dVHdUakiEo4?si=xLZTJvrqEjA4m7Kv Evangelion Collab promotional video], replacing them with the additions of [[Legend Capsules (Gacha Event)|Legend Tickets]], [[Ultra Talents]] and [[Ultra Form|Ultra Forms]].
**Additionally, one of the strangest omissions from the English version is a series of cats at the bottom of the map, most containing gags, aside from [[Meditation Cat (Special Cat)|Meditation Cat]] at the end wishing for a good 11th year. It is unknown why most of them were cut.
***Out of the cats included at the bottom, [[Hikakin (Special Cat)|Hikakin]], [[Cat Student]] and [[Cat Giraffe Modoki (Special Cat)|Cat Giraffe Modoki]] stand out for being Japan-exclusive units, making their omission more understandable, especially for Hikakin's [[Hikakin Collaboration Event|collab]] being with a Japanese YouTuber who is largely unknown outside of Japan and Cat Giraffe Modoki being part of a [[JRA Collaboration Event|collab]] with the Japanese Racing Association.
*The map shows [[Cats of the Cosmos]] before [[Heavenly Tower]], even though Heavenly Tower was added first. It also shows [[True Form]]s after [[Into the Future]], which is inaccurate unless referring to True Forms of [[:Category:Gacha Cats|gacha units]] such as [[Megidora (Uber Rare Cat)|Megidora]].

